  "chunks": [
    {
      "text": "Vellum",
      "start": 0.0,
      "duration": 1.4
    },
    {
      "text": "A river remembering a drawing.",
      "start": 1.58,
      "duration": 2.925
    },
    {
      "text": "Blue, green, and orange pigment move across warm paper, carried by currents that fold into eddies and gather around circular basins. A faint pencil construction gives the water something to follow, and something to escape. Concentrated colour passes into delicate, diluted traces.",
      "start": 4.685,
      "duration": 19.275
    },
    {
      "text": "Release ink, stir the water, or place an eddy. A gesture joins the same currents already moving through the sheet. Change the seed to begin another composition, or hold a moment and save it as a print.",
      "start": 24.14,
      "duration": 13.9
    },
    {
      "text": "The work explores the meeting of a drawn structure and a moving material. The surface holds their traces as the currents keep changing.",
      "start": 38.22,
      "duration": 9.275
    },
    {
      "text": "By Brad Necyk. Previously developed as Capillary. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
      "start": 47.675,
      "duration": 7.025
    }
  ],
